PocketBase works as a normal Go library. You call `pocketbase.New()`, attach handlers to its hooks, and then call `app.Start()`. I checked the signatures below against the PocketBase source in your working directory (`core/base.go`, `core/app.go`, `tools/router`, `apis/middlewares.go`). This is the v0.23+ API, where every hook handler must call `e.Next()`.

### Setup

```sh
mkdir myapp && cd myapp
go mod init myapp
go get github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase
```

### `main.go`

```go
package main

import (
	"log"
	"net/http"

	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase"
	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase/apis"
	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase/core"
)

func main() {
	app := pocketbase.New()

	// --- Custom routes ---------------------------------------------
	app.OnServe().BindFunc(func(se *core.ServeEvent) error {
		// public route: GET /api/hello/{name}
		se.Router.GET("/api/hello/{name}", func(e *core.RequestEvent) error {
			name := e.Request.PathValue("name")
			return e.JSON(http.StatusOK, map[string]string{"message": "Hello " + name})
		})

		// auth-protected route
		se.Router.POST("/api/myapp/whoami", func(e *core.RequestEvent) error {
			return e.JSON(http.StatusOK, map[string]any{"id": e.Auth.Id})
		}).Bind(apis.RequireAuth())

		return se.Next() // required: continues the serve chain
	})

	// --- Record create hook ----------------------------------------
	app.OnRecordCreate("posts").BindFunc(func(e *core.RecordEvent) error {
		// runs BEFORE the insert: change or validate the record here
		if e.Record.GetString("status") == "" {
			e.Record.Set("status", "draft")
		}
		// returning an error here cancels the create, e.g.:
		// return apis.NewBadRequestError("title is required", nil)

		if err := e.Next(); err != nil { // does the actual insert
			return err
		}

		// runs AFTER the insert (may still be inside a transaction)
		log.Println("created post", e.Record.Id)
		return nil
	})

	if err := app.Start(); err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}
}
```

Run it with `go run . serve`. The API and dashboard will be at `http://127.0.0.1:8090`, and you can test the route with `curl localhost:8090/api/hello/world`.

### Things to know

- **Always call `e.Next()`** (or `se.Next()`). If you return without calling it, the chain stops. For `OnServe` the server won't finish starting, and for `OnRecordCreate` the record is never saved.
- **The tag `"posts"`** limits the hook to that collection. It accepts collection names or IDs. With no tags, the hook runs for every collection.
- **Pick the right create hook:**
  - `OnRecordCreate`: runs on every create, whether it comes from the REST API or from your own Go code calling `app.Save(record)`. Use it to set defaults or validate.
  - `OnRecordCreateRequest`: runs only for API create requests. Its `*core.RecordRequestEvent` gives you `e.Auth` and `e.Request`, so use it for checks based on who is calling.
  - `OnRecordAfterCreateSuccess`: runs after the record is committed. Put side effects here, like sending emails or calling webhooks, so they don't fire if a transaction rolls back.
- **Use `e.App` inside handlers**, not the outer `app`, for any database work. That way your queries join the current transaction if one is running.
- **Route paths** use Go 1.22+ `net/http` patterns, such as `{name}` and `{path...}`. Read path values with `e.Request.PathValue(...)`.
- **For route groups**, use `g := se.Router.Group("/api/myapp")`. You can add middleware to a whole group with `g.Bind(apis.RequireAuth())`.

Import PocketBase as a library, create the app with `pocketbase.New()`, register your routes inside an `OnServe()` hook, and attach record hooks with `OnRecordCreate(...)`. This repo is PocketBase itself (v0.23+ API). I built the example below against it and it compiles.

### Setup

```bash
mkdir myapp && cd myapp
go mod init myapp
# add main.go (below), then:
go mod tidy
go run . serve
```

### main.go

```go
package main

import (
	"log"
	"net/http"
	"strings"

	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase"
	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase/apis"
	"github.com/pocketbase/pocketbase/core"
)

func main() {
	app := pocketbase.New()

	// ---- custom routes ----
	app.OnServe().BindFunc(func(se *core.ServeEvent) error {
		// public route
		se.Router.GET("/api/hello/{name}", func(e *core.RequestEvent) error {
			name := e.Request.PathValue("name")
			return e.JSON(http.StatusOK, map[string]string{"message": "Hello " + name})
		})

		// authenticated route that creates a record (this also fires the hooks below)
		se.Router.POST("/api/posts/quick", func(e *core.RequestEvent) error {
			data := struct {
				Title string `json:"title"`
			}{}
			if err := e.BindBody(&data); err != nil {
				return e.BadRequestError("Invalid body", err)
			}

			collection, err := e.App.FindCollectionByNameOrId("posts")
			if err != nil {
				return e.NotFoundError("Missing posts collection", err)
			}

			record := core.NewRecord(collection)
			record.Set("title", data.Title)
			record.Set("author", e.Auth.Id)

			if err := e.App.Save(record); err != nil {
				return e.BadRequestError("Failed to create post", err)
			}

			return e.JSON(http.StatusOK, record)
		}).Bind(apis.RequireAuth())

		return se.Next() // required
	})

	// ---- on-record-create hook ----
	app.OnRecordCreate("posts").BindFunc(func(e *core.RecordEvent) error {
		// before the INSERT: change the record here
		e.Record.Set("slug", strings.ToLower(strings.ReplaceAll(e.Record.GetString("title"), " ", "-")))

		if err := e.Next(); err != nil { // runs the actual INSERT
			return err
		}

		// after the INSERT, but the transaction may not be committed yet
		return nil
	})

	// runs only after the create has been committed
	app.OnRecordAfterCreateSuccess("posts").BindFunc(func(e *core.RecordEvent) error {
		e.App.Logger().Info("New post", "id", e.Record.Id)
		return e.Next()
	})

	if err := app.Start(); err != nil {
		log.Fatal(err)
	}
}
```

### Things to know

- **Always call `e.Next()` / `se.Next()`.** Hooks form a chain, and if you skip `Next()` the rest of the chain never runs. For `OnRecordCreate`, that means the record is never saved.
- **Choosing a create hook:**
  - `OnRecordCreate`: fires on every create, whether it comes from the REST API, the admin dashboard, or your own `app.Save()` calls. Code before `e.Next()` runs before the insert; code after it runs after.
  - `OnRecordAfterCreateSuccess`: fires only after the record is committed. Use it for side effects like emails or webhooks.
  - `OnRecordCreateRequest`: fires only for the REST API create endpoint, and gives you `e.Auth` and the request. Use it for request-specific checks.
- **Tags:** `OnRecordCreate("posts", "comments")` limits the hook to those collections. With no arguments it fires for every collection.
- **Route paths:** routes use Go 1.22+ `net/http` patterns (`{name}`, `{path...}`), read with `e.Request.PathValue("name")`. Put custom routes under `/api/...` to avoid clashing with the admin UI or static files.
- **Route middleware:** `.Bind(apis.RequireAuth())` requires an auth token, and `apis.RequireSuperuserAuth()` requires a superuser. To protect several routes at once, use `se.Router.Group("/api/myprefix")` and call `.Bind(...)` on the group.
- **Running it:** `app.Start()` gives you the normal PocketBase CLI (`serve`, `migrate`, `superuser`, …), so start it with `go run . serve`.

The example assumes a `posts` collection with `title`, `slug`, and `author` fields. Change those names to match your schema.
